  longDescription:
    "AGE OF STEAM is a SEMINAL 2002 RAILROAD BUILDING BOARD GAME designed by MARTIN WALLACE (British game designer known for BRASS BIRMINGHAM 2018, BRASS LANCASHIRE 2007, LONDON, AUTOMOBILE + others) — considered the DEFINING MODERN RAILROAD GAME OUTSIDE THE 18xx GENRE + one of the most influential HEAVY EURO games of the 2000s. PUBLISHER: Warfrog Games (Wallace's own company) initially; later Eagle-Gryphon Games (still current publisher). OVERVIEW: 2-6 players build a RAILROAD EMPIRE across a HEX MAP (default map: Eastern USA + Midwest) by LAYING TRACK connecting cities + DELIVERING CUBES (representing goods of various colors) along their rail networks to earn INCOME + VICTORY POINTS. GAME STRUCTURE: Fixed 10 ROUNDS. Each round follows this sequence: (1) DETERMINE PLAYER ORDER via AUCTION (bidding for turn order priority). (2) SELECT ROLE (unique player action for the round) from: FIRST BUILD, LOCOMOTIVE (increase train range), ENGINEER (build extra track), URBANIZER (upgrade a city), TURN ORDER (choose position next round), and others depending on version — SIGNATURE MECHANIC: each role can only be taken by ONE PLAYER per round. (3) BUILD TRACK (place hex tiles connecting cities) — track costs money based on terrain. (4) DELIVER GOODS (move colored cubes along your track network from cities to destination cities of matching color) — each successful delivery earns income + VP. (5) INCOME PHASE (collect income based on total delivery + track network size). (6) UPGRADE LOCOMOTIVE (buy longer train range). (7) EXPENSES (pay interest on loans + track maintenance). SIGNATURE BRUTAL LOAN SYSTEM: You start with zero money. To do anything you must ISSUE SHARES (take loans) — each share gives $5 but you must PAY $1 INTEREST per share PER ROUND for the rest of the game + they REDUCE YOUR FINAL VP. This creates tremendous tension: borrow enough to grow but not so much you drown in interest. INCOME SCALING: Higher income levels reduce your income growth (bracket-based) — you can't just accelerate forever. GAME END: After 10 rounds; VICTORY POINTS = income + track network bonus - loans; highest VP wins. GAME LENGTH: 2-4 hours. WEIGHT: BoardGameGeek weight ~4.0/5 — very heavy Euro strategy. EXPANSION MAPS: OVER 30 OFFICIAL + FAN-MADE expansion maps covering different regions + rules variations: SWITZERLAND (very tight economy), SCANDINAVIA, JAPAN, INDIA, LONDON (specialized), BARBADOS + BERMUDA (tiny map, tight play), FRANCE (bureaucratic complexity), and many more. Each map introduces UNIQUE RULES + STRATEGIC WRINKLES making the base game endlessly replayable. Modern edition: STEAM (2009, Mayfair Games) is a simplified re-implementation for lighter play; AGE OF STEAM DELUXE (2020, Eagle-Gryphon) is the current premium edition with high-quality components. INFLUENCE: Age of Steam established the modern 'CUBE DELIVERY' + 'TRACK-LAYING' Euro subgenre; inspired STEAM (2009), RAILWAYS OF THE WORLD (2005), and many others. Considered a MASTERPIECE OF WALLACE'S OEUVRE alongside Brass Birmingham. RANKINGS: BoardGameGeek Top 200 (peaked around #100-200); regularly features in 'best Euro game' lists.",
